%N A397766 Primes of the form x^^y + w^^y, where x, y, w >= 2 and ^^ denotes tetration.
%C A397766 Subsequence of A393643.
%C A397766 For any integer m > 0, x^^y + w^^y <= m implies x^^y < m and w^^y < m. Hence, all terms of the present sequence that are smaller than or equal to m can be obtained by considering only tetrations x^^y < m and pairing those having the same height y.
%e A397766 a(6) = 2^^3 + 3^^3.
